fix the @ modifier scope in lineparser.cpp


In BeebAsm, FOR loops, {} blocks, and Macros all use the exact same underlying scoping mechanism (a stack of scopes). By modifying how the assignment logic works for @, we fix the behavior for all of them simultaneously.

Here is why this works globally:

FOR Loops: As you saw, it allows updating a loop counter or accumulator defined outside the loop.
{ } Blocks: If you have a variable defined outside a {} block, var@ = val inside the block will now correctly update the outer variable instead of creating a shadowed local one.
Macros: Macros in BeebAsm run in their own scope (implicitly wrapped in {}). This fix allows a macro to update a variable passed to it or defined in the context where the macro was called, which is essential for macros that act as "functions" modifying state.

